file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__orient(args: { [key: string]: unknown; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__why\",\"description\":\"Explain a symbol or file: definition, callers/callees with confidence origins, files that historically change with it (N/M commits: N shared, M counted in the mined window), commits that explain it.\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__why(args: {\\n  // symbol name, FQN, or repo-relative file path\\n  query: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006","create_time":1794862847.238677}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":9,"sampled_through_sequence":5,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
